  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n\n// Process\n\nHow a project runs, week by week. \n\nNo big reveal at the end. You see working software every Friday, and you always know what moved and why.\n\nStart a project\nSee the services\n\nBefore\n\n01 / 06\n\nThe first call\n\nThirty minutes. You describe the product and the deadline. I ask about the team, the codebase and what has already been tried.\n\nYou get\n\nA written quote within two working days\n\nWeek 0\n\n02 / 06\n\nArchitecture note\n\nTwo pages: routes, data flow, state, what gets tested and what does not. Nothing is built until you have signed it off.\n\nYou get\n\nThe note, a timeline and a price range\n\nWeek 1\n\n03 / 06\n\nFirst deploy\n\nA real screen on a real URL behind a login, with CI, a preview for every pull request and the performance budget switched on.\n\nYou get\n\nA link you can open on your phone\n\nWeeks 2 to 6\n\n04 / 06\n\nOne flow a week\n\nEach flow is finished before the next one starts: components, empty and error states, tests. You never wait for a big reveal.\n\nYou get\n\nA Friday build and a short written update\n\nWeek 7\n\n05 / 06\n\nHardening\n\nReal devices, slow networks, keyboard only. The numbers are read at the 75th percentile, not on my laptop.\n\nYou get\n\nA before and after report\n\nLast week\n\n06 / 06\n\nHandover\n\nDocs in the repository, a recorded walkthrough and a call with whoever maintains it next.\n\nYou get\n\nThe docs, the recording and thirty days of questions\n\n// The length changes from project to project. The order does not.\n\n// Questions\n\nAsked before every project. \n\nSomething else?\n\nReplies within one working day\n\nAsk by email\n01\nWhen are you available?\n\nI take on one main project at a time and usually book four to six weeks ahead. The status line at the top of the site is kept up to date.\n\n02\nDo you work alone or with a team?\n03\nHow do you price a project?\n04\nDo you only work in React?\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n--:--\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.",
